    icon: '💡',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Take exactly one trick. Once you have captured one trick containing a low point card (like a King or a 3), stop winning. Leading small cards (4s and 5s) for the rest of the game is the safest way to stay in the 'middle' bracket.\n\nDump your Aces. Because an Ace is worth 3 points, it is a dangerous liability. Try to play your Aces early into tricks led by others, especially if you cannot win the trick.\n\nThe Outlier Trap: If you see a player has 0 points and it's near the end, lead a suit they *must* follow to force them to win a trick. This protects you from being the 'low' loser and forces them into the game.",
    Player: "Take exactly one trick. Once you have captured one trick containing a low point card (like a King or a 3), stop winning. Leading small cards (4s and 5s) for the rest of the game is the safest way to stay in the 'middle' bracket.\n\nDump your Aces. Because an Ace is worth 3 points, it is a dangerous liability. Try to play your Aces early into tricks led by others, especially if you cannot win the trick.\n\nThe Outlier Trap: If you see a player has 0 points and it's near the end, lead a suit they *must* follow to force them to win a trick. This protects you from being the 'low' loser and forces them into the game.",
